   <media:description>Caltech created the Jet Propulsion Laboratory in 1936. Decades in the making, this has brought the United States a long line of firsts. Together, Caltech and JPL advance frontier technologies - including quantum, AI and autonomy, microelectronics, advanced radar and sensing, robotics, and resilient space systems - with applications across civil, defense, intelligence, and commercial sectors. Caltech JPL helps sustain America’s innovation edge and the capabilities essential to long-term strategic advantage.

Learn more: https://www.caltech.edu/research/jpl</media:description>
